We will deploy NGINX.

Step 15. Create an NGINX Deployment
On Master:
kubectl create deployment nginx --image=nginx

Check:
kubectl get deployments

kubectl get pods -o wide

Explain how Kubernetes schedules the Pod on an available Worker node.
Step 16. Scale the application
kubectl scale deployment nginx --replicas=3

Verify:
kubectl get pods -o wide

Students should observe where the three Pods are running.
Step 17. Expose the application
kubectl expose deployment nginx \
--type=NodePort \
--port=80

Check:
kubectl get svc

Example:
NAME    TYPE       CLUSTER-IP      EXTERNAL-IP   PORT(S)
nginx   NodePort   10.96.100.20    <none>        80:31234/TCP

Now access:
http://WORKER_PRIVATE_IP:31234

For EC2, configure the Security Group to permit the required NodePort traffic from your authorized client IP.

Step 18. Test scaling
kubectl scale deployment nginx --replicas=5

Verify:
kubectl get pods -o wide

Step 19. Delete application
kubectl delete deployment nginx

kubectl delete service nginx
